\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces Wing structure showing the hollow internal geometry with channels for carbon fiber spars (left) and printed aerodynamic shell (right). Each wing weighs approximately 176\,g including carbon reinforcement.\relax }}{14}{figure.caption.11}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.2}{\ignorespaces Wing endcap component serving as motor mount and landing foot. This multi-functional part positions the motor ahead of the leading edge with $\pm 5^{\circ }$ tilt for yaw control and extends downward to protect the wing trailing edge during landing.\relax }}{15}{figure.caption.12}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.3}{\ignorespaces Central core structure that clamps the carbon fiber spars. Two identical cores are used: one houses the ESC, flight controller, and batteries (top), while the other serves as a structural clamp for the lower spars (bottom).\relax }}{15}{figure.caption.13}%
